Instanta is a global coffee manufacturer with more than 20 years of experience, supplying private-label and B2B customers across international markets.

As part of the launch of our new UK operation in Redditch, we are looking for a reliable and well organised person to take responsibility for the day-to-day operation of the warehouse and actively support the packing operations.

*Your role*

You will be responsible for ensuring that goods are received, stored, prepared and dispatched accurately, safely and on time as well as supporting the packing line.

*Location:* Unit 14, The IO Centre, Nash Road, Redditch, B98 7AS

*Shift/ hours: *Days based, with flexibility required (08:00 - 16:00, 37.5 hrs/ week).

*Pay Rate:* competitive

*Key responsibilities:*

* managing the daily receipt, storage and dispatch of goods;
* loading/ unloading & checking deliveries against transport and warehouse documentation;
* preparing customer orders for collection and shipment;
* maintaining accurate stock records and supporting regular stock counts;
* organising warehouse space and ensuring correct product identification and stock rotation;
* coordinating loading, unloading and cooperation with transport companies;
* preparing and maintaining warehouse and dispatch documentation;
* reporting stock discrepancies, damaged goods and operational issues;
* supporting packing, fulfilment and other operational activities at the Redditch site;
* maintaining high standards of organisation, hygiene and workplace safety;
* cooperating with the UK sales team, logistics partners and Instanta’s teams in Poland;
* supporting the implementation and improvement of warehouse procedures as the UK operation develops.

*What we are looking for*

* practical experience in warehouse, logistics, stock management or goods-handling operations
