Location: London NW1 7AN

Salary: £20,000 - £22,000 per annum dependant on experience

About the company:

Comptons is an innovative, award winning, driven and well-established firm of solicitors situated near Regent's Park in North West London.

Comptons are currently recruiting for an Receptionist / Office Assistant to assist in a variety of administrative tasks as well as provide support in the efficient running of the firm’s reception.

Duties of the Receptionist / Office Assistant:

* Receiving all clients and other visitors to the firm in a helpful, friendly and professional manner;
* Process all incoming calls without delay and in an effective manner including the conveying of messages to other members of staff by email. The firm has a Call Centre that is subscribes to and whenever possible we should take calls and deal with them promptly and courteously;
* Photocopying; faxing, scanning and binding of documents and generally dealing with the administration/up-keep of the photocopier/ facsimile/scanner machines on all four floors of the office.
* Postal duties such as preparing letters to go out (putting letters in envelopes and using franking machine), Attending at the post office each day with Recorded Deliveries and delivering post by hand in the local area when required to do so;
* Collection and delivery of the DX post (when required to do so);
* Checking the trays of the internal post system regularly and to deliver post/files/boxes to other floors/departments as and when required;
* Occasionally you will be required to deliver documents to the local Court;
* Regularly check stationery supplies and provide a list to the main receptionist.
* To buy kitchen supplies when necessary such as Coffee, Tea, Milk etc.
* Provide refreshments when requested to do so including Partners meetings lunch orders.

This list is not exhaustive, and the Receptionist / Office Assistant might be required to assist with other duties such as:

* Assisting the accounts department with inputting data;
* Social media and marketing research.

Requirements of the Receptionist / Office Assistant:

* Previous Administrative experience is desirable however full training will be given as part of this role;
* Computer literacy with proficiency in the Microsoft Office Suite;
* A good command of English both written and spoken;
* Good communication and listening skills;
* Client Service Orientation;
* Organisation skills;
* Time Management skills;
* Dependability and reliability;
* Confidentiality;
* A good team player with a positive attitude
