Position Overview

BibliU is looking for two Senior Accountants to take end to end ownership of core accounting processes across our multi-entity group. This role sits close to the detail: closing the books accurately every month, partnering across Finance, Legal, Tax, and Treasury to get accounting treatment right, and spotting where controls or processes need to improve before they become a problem. You will report to the Corporate Controller and be a key driver of the accuracy and scalability of our accounting function as the group grows.

What you will be doing:

Perform and manage monthly, quarterly, and annual close activities, including reconciliations, journal entries, and financial statement preparation across group entities;
Support the preparation, review, and filing of external financial reports as applicable to the group's reporting obligations;
Take end to end ownership of accounting processes and projects, exercising judgment to keep the close moving and ensure the right decisions get made under time pressure;
Partner with Finance, Legal, Tax, Treasury, and other cross functional stakeholders to understand business initiatives and assess their accounting implications;
Assess the effectiveness of controls in your area and contribute to the design of new controls as the business grows and processes evolve;
Identify and implement process improvement and automation opportunities that improve efficiency, accuracy, and scalability across the accounting function;
Research and document technical accounting positions on significant or non routine transactions;
Assess risk and internal control considerations, escalating issues to leadership with clear context and recommendations;
Analyze complex processes and financial data to identify root causes and surface actionable insights.

What we are looking for

Must Have

Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field;
5 to 10 years of progressive accounting experience, including ownership of month end and quarter end close;
Solid understanding of accounting principles and financial reporting, with exposure to more than one jurisdiction (multi-entity experience a strong plus);
Advanced Excel skills: reconciliations, complex formulas, and data analysis;
Comfortable using AI tools to improve accuracy or efficiency in day to day accounting work;
Strong written and verbal communication skills, with experience partnering across departments such as Legal, Tax, or Treasury;
Demonstrated ability to research and document technical accounting positions;
Sound judgment and ability to make timely decisions to keep close deadlines on track;
Strong attention to detail and a proactive approach to identifying and escalating risk.

Good to Have

ACCA (or equivalent professional accounting qualification), a plus rather than a requirement;
Experience supporting external financial reporting or statutory filings;
Direct experience with Iplicit or similar multi-entity accounting systems;
Experience working in a fast-growing business;
Exposure to process automation or systems implementation projects.

