JOIN OUR BRAND-NEW DONCASTER OFFICE

*16 Hours Per Week – Exciting Startup Opportunity*

Home-Care Perfection Limited is opening a brand-new office in Doncaster, and we are looking for an experienced, confident and enthusiastic Care/Support Worker to join us at the beginning of this exciting new venture.

This is a unique opportunity to help build and develop a new local care service from the ground up.

The position will initially be 16 hours per week. As this is a new office, we will initially be building our client base, so there may not be enough care hours available to fill all 16 hours.

During this startup period, the successful candidate will be expected to use some of their contracted hours to help grow the business. This will include leaflet distribution across different areas of Doncaster, promoting our services and speaking with members of the local community and potential clients.

As the client base grows, we expect the role to develop, with more hours being spent providing care and opportunities for additional hours, increased responsibility and career progression.

*This role would suit someone who is:*

· Experienced in providing care and able to work independently and on their own initiative;

· Confident, outgoing, friendly and approachable;

· Comfortable speaking with members of the public and potential clients;

· Able to confidently answer questions about care and our services or know when to seek further information;

· Flexible and willing to take on different responsibilities as the new office develops;

· Reliable, organised and professional;

· Caring, compassionate and sensitive to the needs of others;

· A good communicator with good spoken English;

· Able to travel around Doncaster using their own car.

WHY JOIN US?

*Be Part of Something New* – You will be joining our Doncaster office at the very beginning and will have the opportunity to play an important role in establishing the business within the local community.

*Grow With the Business* – As our Doncaster client base develops, there may be opportunities for additional working hours, increased care responsibilities, career progression, senior or supervisory opportunities, and training and professional development.

*Training and Qualifications* – We invest in our staff and offer ongoing training and support. There may be opportunities to work towards funded NVQ qualifications from Level 2–5, subject to eligibility and company requirements.

*Make a Difference* – Our approach is centred around putting people first. You will help people remain safely and comfortably in their own homes while supporting their dignity, independence and quality of life.

ABOUT HOME-CARE PERFECTION LIMITED

Having experienced first-hand the importance of quality care within the home environment, we understand how important it is for families to have confidence in the people caring for their loved ones.

We want to change the approach to care in the UK by putting people first and providing compassionate, reliable and personalised care.

Our carers are central to everything we do. We value their commitment and recognise the important role they play within the community.

Our aim is to enable as many people as possible to remain in their own homes for as long as possible, while giving families peace of mind that their loved ones are in capable and caring hands.

THE ROLE

As a Care/Support Worker, you will provide personalised care and support to service users in their own homes in accordance with their individual Care Plans.

You will be expected to work independently while maintaining high standards of care, respecting each service user's dignity, privacy, independence and choices at all times.

*Main responsibilities include:*

· Providing personal and practical care to people with a range of illnesses and disabilities;

· Supporting with washing, bathing, dressing, toileting and personal care;

· Supporting service users with mobility and the use of personal equipment;

· Providing companionship and supporting mental and physical wellbeing;

· Preparing light meals and assisting with eating where required;

· Light household duties such as making beds, tidying rooms and laundry;

· Palliative care where required and appropriately trained;

· Following individual care plans and management instructions;

· Maintaining accurate daily care records and medication documentation;

· Logging arrival and departure times accurately for every visit;

· Reporting changes in health, behaviour or circumstances to management;

· Reporting accidents, incidents and safeguarding or care concerns;

· Following all company policies, Health & Safety and infection control procedures;

· Maintaining confidentiality and complying with the Data Protection Act 2018 and UK GDPR;

· Participating in training, supervision, care reviews and appraisals;

· Carrying out other reasonable duties required by management.

MARKETING & COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT

Because this is a new Doncaster office, you will also be expected to help establish our presence within the local community.

· Distributing company leaflets in different areas of Doncaster;

· Promoting our home-care services;

· Speaking confidently and professionally with members of the public;

· Answering basic questions about our services;

· Helping generate awareness of Home-Care Perfection Limited;

· Supporting local marketing and business development activities.

You must therefore be confident approaching people, comfortable having conversations and able to represent the company professionally.

WORKING HOURS & FLEXIBILITY

The role will initially be 16 hours per week.

The balance between care work and marketing/business development will depend on the number of clients we have while the Doncaster office is being established.

The successful candidate must be flexible and willing to undertake different duties and work the hours and days reasonably required by the company, subject to the agreed terms of employment and appropriate notice.

As the client base grows, there may be opportunities for additional working hours.

ESSENTIAL EXPERIENCE & REQUIREMENTS

We are looking for an experienced Care/Support Worker who is confident working independently.

In summary

*Essential:*

· Previous experience working in a care/support role;

· Experience providing care to vulnerable adults;

· Ability to work independently and use your own initiative;

· Own car and full driving licence;

· Good spoken English;

· Confident communication skills;

· Friendly, outgoing and approachable personality;

· Comfortable speaking with members of the public and potential clients;

· Ability to answer questions confidently and professionally;

· Reliable and trustworthy;

· Flexible and adaptable;

· Professional attitude and appearance;

· Commitment to providing high-quality, person-centred care.

*Desirable:*

· NVQ/QCF Level 2 or 3 in Health and Social Care;

· Experience working in domiciliary/home care;

· Experience with medication administration;

· Experience supporting people with complex care needs.

CAREER DEVELOPMENT

We believe in developing our staff from within the organisation. As the Doncaster branch grows, the right candidate will have the opportunity to grow with it. Performance, commitment, skills and willingness to develop will be considered when opportunities for additional responsibility and progression arise.

We may also support eligible employees to work towards funded NVQ qualifications from Level 2–5.

FLEXIBILITY

This job description provides a broad outline of the main responsibilities of the role.

As this is a new startup office, the successful candidate must be flexible and adaptable as the Doncaster branch develops.

The balance of care, marketing, community and administrative duties may change as the business grows.

The post-holder may also be required to undertake other reasonable duties appropriate to their role and experience.

