Role Description

We are seeking a capable and detail-oriented Accountant to join our growing organisation. This is a full-time, office-based position located in Dartford, Kent.

The Accountant will be responsible for overseeing the company’s day-to-day financial operations and maintaining accurate, timely and compliant financial records.

Key responsibilities will include:

* Managing accounts payable and accounts receivable;
* Preparing and issuing invoices and monitoring outstanding payments;
* Maintaining accurate general ledger entries;
* Processing and verifying payroll information;
* Reconciling bank accounts and investigating discrepancies;
* Supporting month-end and year-end closing procedures;
* Preparing management accounts, financial statements and internal reports;
* Assisting with budgets, cash-flow forecasts and financial planning;
* Monitoring expenditure and helping management maintain effective cost controls;
* Supporting external accountants, auditors and regulatory reviews;
* Ensuring compliance with applicable UK financial regulations, tax requirements and internal controls;
* Maintaining organised records and appropriate audit trails; and
* Working closely with management, operational teams and care coordinators to provide financial information that supports effective decision-making and high-quality, person-centred services.

The successful candidate must be comfortable working within a growing organisation and capable of improving financial processes, maintaining strong controls and providing management with clear and reliable financial information.

Qualifications and Experience

The ideal candidate will have:

* Strong accounting and bookkeeping skills, including experience in general ledger management, bank reconciliations and accounts payable and receivable;
* Experience preparing management accounts, budgets, forecasts and financial reports;
* Proficiency in recognised accounting software and, ideally, experience using ERP systems;
* Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including formulas, pivot tables and financial data analysis;
* A sound understanding of UK financial regulations, taxation principles, payroll requirements and audit processes;
* Excellent numerical, analytical and problem-solving abilities;
* Exceptional attention to detail and a commitment to accuracy;
* Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritise competing responsibilities and meet deadlines;
* Effective written and verbal communication skills;
* The ability to work collaboratively with finance, management, operational and care teams;
* A high level of integrity, discretion and confidentiality when handling sensitive financial and employee information; and
* A degree or relevant professional qualification in Accounting, Finance or a related discipline.

ACA, ACCA or CIMA accreditation—whether part-qualified or fully qualified—would be advantageous. Previous accounting experience within healthcare, social care, domiciliary care, supported living or another service-based organisation would also be highly desirable.

